From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Gino D." <25200363+zinosaure@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 23:51:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] gameflex: the queue backpressure case of upstream 2d97fb50 is
 not run

It pushes a blocking empty block then a non-blocking one and expects the second refused; since
gameflex 0031 a blocking push returns once the queue has room again, so the second one fits.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 tests/AudioOut2PortTests.cpp | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tests/AudioOut2PortTests.cpp b/tests/AudioOut2PortTests.cpp
index b8357a65..6ac7f9e3 100644
--- a/tests/AudioOut2PortTests.cpp
+++ b/tests/AudioOut2PortTests.cpp
@@ -963,7 +963,9 @@ int main() {
 	TestSynchronousDevicePushBypassesModelledQueue();
 	TestFloat12ChannelPortOutputsPcm();
 	TestAsynchronousDevicePushKeepsQueueBounded();
-	TestHandleWithoutPcmDoesNotBypassQueue();
+	// GameFlex: not run. A blocking push returns once the queue has room again (gameflex 0031, as the console's
+	// output does), so the non-blocking push after it finds room: this upstream case assumes the opposite.
+	(void)TestHandleWithoutPcmDoesNotBypassQueue;
 	TestPushConsumesPcm();
 	TestQueueDrainsAtExactGrainRate();
 	TestQueueLevelResults();
